ory_tweet_ids": ["2120484028327584082"], "id": "2120484028327584082", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 26, "impression_count": 8255, "like_count": 88, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 6}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120449543141511586", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Peasants as a project of intellectual history. This looks absolutely fascinating! https://t.co/R3WyxryhZT", "url": "https://x.com/adam_tooze/status/2120484028327584082"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T10:55:14.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120470401738531106"], "id": "2120470401738531106", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 37, "impression_count": 44795, "like_count": 72, "quote_count": 5, "reply_count": 9, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "NEW ODD LOTS:\n\nA brutal 5 weeks for hedge funds of all types.\n\n@tracyalloway and I talk to @nishantkumar07 about all these funds posting terrible numbers and then we also talk to Bloomberg News’ Michael Ball about what’s driving these huge market moves  https://t.co/0iQUJrpW7G", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120470401738531106"}, {"author_id": "14096763", "created_at": "2026-11-11T10:38:04.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120466078077755778"], "id": "2120466078077755778", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 13221, "like_count": 60, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 5}, "text": "$CRWV +12% pre-market", "url": "https://x.com/TheStalwart/status/2120466078077755778"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T07:05:03.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120412471664300411"], "id": "2120412471664300411", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 4960, "like_count": 19, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 1}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120088833681231991", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Does anyone know what this chart is actually showing?\n\nIt’s not “real average hourly earnings” as indicated but *is* some sort of transformation of nominal average hourly earnings https://t.co/ewlZxz0XGj", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120412471664300411"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:47:01.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120332438203449588"], "id": "2120332438203449588", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 0, "impression_count": 2196, "like_count": 4, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 1}, "text": "1/ The October Main Street Health Report from @joinhomebase is out:\n\nhttps://t.co/3hHl5cPBDE", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120332438203449588"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:36:19.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120329743904219257"], "id": "2120329743904219257", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 7, "impression_count": 10575, "like_count": 69, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 10, "retweet_count": 13}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120279670562406900", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "I thought it was well understood that the issue isn't that China's exports are exceptionally high as a share of GDP, but rather than China exports are especially high relative to its imports, especially of manufactures\n\n(chip price surge impacting both sides of the ledger now) https://t.co/O2pA8pADEj https://t.co/vR7OBIO1c7", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120329743904219257"}, {"author_id": "733647469305864195", "created_at": "2026-11-11T01:04:53.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120321833878913057"], "id": "2120321833878913057", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 28, "impression_count": 14766, "like_count": 133, "quote_count": 3, "reply_count": 17, "retweet_count": 32}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120320387653456082", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "The core issue is that China has been all exports and no imports for the last 6 years, and there is no sign that is changing\n\n1/3 https://t.co/Kq2KJbPFig https://t.co/9H14BRRSXJ", "url": "https://x.com/Brad_Setser/status/2120321833878913057"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-10T23:23:45.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120296380686303405"], "id": "2120296380686303405", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 2, "impression_count": 3014, "like_count": 26, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 3, "retweet_count": 0}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120265450483282363", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "To broaden Matt's comment -\n\nIt's up to you how literally you interpret voters' clamor for lower prices but...\n\nSome items I've seen folks pitch as part of the \"affordability agenda\" are likely to raise not lower prices https://t.co/Pmt42Quf5p", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120296380686303405"}, {"author_id": "497231011", "created_at": "2026-11-10T22:25:13.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120281652568154381"], "id": "2120281652568154381", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 1, "impression_count": 2601, "like_count": 10, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 0, "retweet_count": 4}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120249927603216889", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "Must not be a clear enough case yet. https://t.co/5ghm1VS8vB", "url": "https://x.com/ChinaBeigeBook/status/2120281652568154381"}, {"author_id": "3512101", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:21:46.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120250584909668474"], "id": "2120250584909668474", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 11, "impression_count": 5906, "like_count": 53, "quote_count": 2, "reply_count": 1, "retweet_count": 16}, "referenced_tweets": [{"id": "2120249927603216889", "type": "quoted"}], "text": "\"Several US government agencies pushed for Singapore-based Megaspeed to be included on the so-called entity list of groups connected to China that allegedly posed national security risks, according to multiple people familiar with the deliberations.   But the commerce department, https://t.co/b0e9xylMFJ", "url": "https://x.com/niubi/status/2120250584909668474"}, {"author_id": "961132338", "created_at": "2026-11-10T20:09:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120247402200527244"], "id": "2120247402200527244", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 27, "impression_count": 21691, "like_count": 283, "quote_count": 4, "reply_count": 5, "retweet_count": 30}, "text": "I am not a politics guy, but seriously enforcing chip export controls in the wake of these Nvidia shenanigans seems to hit the sweet spot of:\n\n--Punishing corruption and self-dealing\n--Being rigorous on national security\n--Improving affordability for Americans (on the margin)", "url": "https://x.com/M_C_Klein/status/2120247402200527244"}, {"author_id": "917683048782503937", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:28:37.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120237210687672738"], "id": "2120237210687672738", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 18, "impression_count": 9689, "like_count": 70, "quote_count": 1, "reply_count": 6, "retweet_count": 13}, "text": "Caixin: “Growth in traditional labor-intensive exports slowed again after several months of improvement. Clothing, textiles, luggage and toy exports all lost momentum, as did household appliances.”\n\nEven though China has among the lowest unit labor costs in the world,", "url": "https://x.com/michaelxpettis/status/2120237210687672738"}, {"author_id": "702235316812275712", "created_at": "2026-11-10T19:15:07.000Z", "edit_history_tweet_ids": ["2120233813091737923"], "id": "2120233813091737923", "public_metrics": {"bookmark_count": 3, "impression_count": 6666, "like_count": 50, "quote_count": 0, "reply_count": 7, "retweet_count": 7}, "text": "Bad inflation now probably means worse labor market later :(", "url": "https://x.com/EconBerger/status/2120233813091737923"}], "includes": {"users": [{"id": "2961589380", "name": "Liz Ann Sonders", "username": "LizAnnSonders"}, {"id": "14096763", "name": "Joe Weisenthal", "username": "TheStalwart"}, {"id": "3311286493", "name": "Adam Tooze", "username": "adam_tooze"}, {"id": "702235316812275712", "name": "Guy Berger", "username": "EconBerger"}, {"id": "733647469305864195", "name": "Brad Setser", "username": "Brad_Setser"}, {"id": "497231011", "name": "China Beige Book", "username": "ChinaBeigeBook"}, {"id": "3512101", "name": "Bill Bishop", "username": "niubi"}, {"id": "961132338", "name": "Matthew C. Klein", "username": "M_C_Klein"}, {"id": "917683048782503937", "name": "Michael Pettis", "username": "michaelxpettis"}]}, "meta": {"newest_id": "2120489631934292054", "next_token": "b26v89c19zqg8o3juzovc23py2kiip6qvn4ao65p6j3i5", "oldest_id": "2120233813091737923", "result_count": 25}}
